================================================================================
Event loop: offload blocking route handlers + keep OBO identity in run_blocking
================================================================================

Context:
Request logs (5 rotated files) showed 306 event-loop stalls: 3+ requests
finishing at the same instant with identical durations. The culprits are
`async def` handlers with no `await` that perform synchronous Lakebase /
Databricks REST I/O on the loop (e.g. /settings/registry/bridges p50 14.1 s,
/domain/documents/list, /domain/version-status, /review/my-tasks), freezing
every concurrent request including /navbar/state.
While preparing the change, run_blocking was found to drop ContextVars: it
used loop.run_in_executor() without copying the context, so in Databricks App
mode any code reached through it saw an empty RequestIdentity
(get_data_plane_client() would raise AuthorizationError; Delta reads in
graphdb/delta/Base.py silently fell back to the service principal).

Changes:
1. src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py
   - run_blocking executes the call inside contextvars.copy_context() (same
     semantics as asyncio.to_thread), so the on-behalf-of identity and other
     request-scoped ContextVars are visible in the worker thread.
2. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   - Offloaded via run_blocking: list_domains (/domain/list-projects),
     get_version_status, list_version_details, get_edit_lock,
     release_edit_lock, renew_edit_lock, list_documents.
3. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   - Offloaded: get_current_config, list_registry_domains,
     list_registry_bridges, get_default_emoji, get_analytics_job_enabled,
     teams_matrix, get_delta_warehouse, get_graph_engine_config,
     list_schedules.
4. src/api/routers/internal/review.py
   - Offloaded: my_tasks, review_detail (run_blocking import added).
5. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   - Offloaded: get_graph_metrics_summary, databricks_build_info.
   Handlers stay `async def` (coding rules §5); single-call bodies become
   `await run_blocking(fn, ...)`, multi-statement bodies move into a local
   `_work()` closure. Logic and error mapping are unchanged.
6. tests/units/core/test_run_blocking_context.py (new)
   - RequestIdentity visible inside run_blocking; worker-side ContextVar
     changes do not leak back to the caller.

