================================================================================
Original Graph build for every backend; internal reads default to it
================================================================================

Context:
Steps (c1) and (c2) of the two-phase graph. The internal build
(`/dtwin/sync/start` and `/dtwin/databricks-build/start`) now builds the
Original Graph for every domain, whatever its backend: gateway VIEW, then
`…_data` as a pass-through VIEW, then Delta companions. It no longer loads
Lakebase / Neo4j (the certified build does), never materializes `…_data`,
and drops the legacy `…_inferred` table and `…_graph` view (enrichments live
in the Certified Graph). The Explorer-family routes read the Original Graph
by default: an empty source and the "live" / "live:inferred" tokens map to
it. Graph analytics always snapshots `…_data`, now a view for every domain.
The external build and the scheduled build still use the legacy pipeline
until (c3).

